        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e2ba5d99-b002-5d8b-bf1a-541c41c2d50a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lindka Cierach, Helen Mirren, Sarah Ferguson, Prince Andrew, Lady Victoria Hervey, Cherie Blair\n- Organizations: British Royal Family, European Royal Families, Royal Shakespeare Company\n- Works: The Queen, Wedding dress of Sarah Ferguson\n- Concepts: Triple Crown of Acting, Academy Award for Best Actress\n\nFacts:\n- In 1967, Helen Mirren began her acting career with the Royal Shakespeare Company.\n- Lindka Cierach's notable clients include members of British and European Royal Families, Helen Mirren, Lady Victoria Hervey, and Cherie Blair.\n- Helen Mirren is one of the few performers to achieve the Triple Crown of Acting.\n- In 2007, Helen Mirren won the Academy Award for Best Actress for playing Queen Elizabeth II in The Queen after receiving two previous nominations.\n- Lindka Cierach designed Sarah Ferguson's wedding dress.\n- The beadwork on Sarah Ferguson's wedding dress included hearts for romance, anchors and waves for Prince Andrew's sailing background, and bumblebees and thistles from Sarah Ferguson's family crest.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
